          en: 'The quality of communication between the entrepreneur and the development team is one of the most determining factors for a project\'s success and investment adequacy. Poorly communicated requirements generate rework. Misaligned expectations generate frustration. Undocumented scope changes generate unexpected costs. Clear, frequent, and documented communication is the antidote for most problems that inflate software project costs.\n\nThe entrepreneur who invests time in clearly communicating what they need, who actively participates in intermediate validations, who provides quick and constructive feedback, and who keeps expectations aligned with project reality, is investing directly in development efficiency. On the other hand, the entrepreneur who delegates everything, who doesn\'t follow progress, who frequently changes their mind without considering impact, and who expects results that were never agreed upon, is ensuring the project will cost more than it should.',
